pg_duckdb: re-sync the vendored PG 19 ruleutils with PG 19 as released

pg_duckdb vendors PostgreSQL's deparser per major (src/vendor/pg_ruleutils_19.c,
added by upstream PR #983 and unchanged on upstream main as of ee38d3b). The
snapshot it was copied from predates two PostgreSQL changes made during the 19
beta cycle:

  * postgres 372b8d1 (2026-07-17) Revert "Add GROUP BY ALL" - Query.groupByAll
    no longer exists;
  * postgres 2a9541d (2026-07-27) "Deparse FOR PORTION OF using the range
    column's current name" - ForPortionOfExpr.range_name became rangeVar (a
    Var), with the column name resolved from the target RTE.

Upstream's PG19 CI cell was green at their last main run (2026-07-17 12:03 UTC,
minutes before the first of those commits) and main has had no run since, so the
staleness is invisible there. Against released PG 19 the file fails to compile
("Query has no member named groupByAll"), which blocks the whole extension.
The hunks below mirror PG 19's own src/backend/utils/adt/ruleutils.c.

The file is wrapped in `#if PG_VERSION_NUM >= 190000 && < 200000`, so the patch
is a no-op for PG 16/17/18 builds. Drop it once upstream refreshes the vendored
copy; `git apply --check` in the build will fail loudly when that happens.

